/// Computes the loss given a cost price and a selling price.
/// 
/// If the cost price is strictly greater than the selling price,
/// the loss is the difference between them. Otherwise, the loss is zero.
/// 
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `cost_price` - Non-negative integer representing the cost price.
/// * `selling_price` - Non-negative integer representing the selling price.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// The computed loss as an `i32`.
fn calculate_loss(cost_price: i32, selling_price: i32) -> i32 {
    if cost_price > selling_price {
        cost_price - selling_price
    } else {
        0
    }
}

